From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:57:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Add a rounding-preserving live-replay GDN decode kernel
 (SGLANG_GDN_EXACT_REPLAY)

With --enable-linear-replayssm and an FP32 state, the ring stores the packed
decode's own FP32 operands (normalized key, raw value, g, beta) and each step
replays them from the dense anchor in the packed kernel's order before
processing the current token, so outputs and anchors are meant to be
bit-identical to the packed decode while the state is written only every
--linear-replayssm-cache-len steps (state traffic 2D -> D + D/L).
